Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ScrollLock (scancode 0x46) -> F24 (scancode 0x76)
;
; The client's console hotkey is IK_F24 (Engine.Console.ConsoleHotKey=135) and
; ConsoleHotKey is not a config variable, so it cannot be changed from an ini.
; User.ini key binds do not work either -- the client sets its bindings at
; runtime via setinput_BD. That leaves sending a real F24, which no normal
; keyboard has.
;
; This maps it in the keyboard class driver, below the injected-input APIs the
; client rejects, so the keystroke is indistinguishable from any other physical
; key. Machine-wide, needs a reboot, and ScrollLock stops being ScrollLock until
; f24-off.reg is applied.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Keyboard Layout]
"Scancode Map"=hex:00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,02,00,00,00,76,00,46,00,00,00,00,00
